      trade="Engineered Wood Framing"
      content="Nailing two plies of 1-3/4-inch LVL together with standard 16d common nails requires 2 rows of nails spaced 12 inches on center driven from both sides. To save hours of hand-nailing and avoid splitting, use code-approved 2-7/8-inch structural screws (FastenMaster HeadLOK or Simpson Strong-Drive SDWS). Driven from one side only in 2 rows at 16 inches on center, they draw the plies together with immense clamping force."
    />
  </div>

